WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.448 --> 00:00:02.990
All the stuff you
see in video games,

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:06.324
we're gonna show you how
to do in real life.

00:00:06.324 --> 00:00:08.862
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:08.862 --> 00:00:10.820
ANNOUNCER: One of the
most recognizable figures

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:12.013
in the sports world.

00:00:12.013 --> 00:00:13.430
ANNOUNCER: There's
one name that's

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:16.180
synonymous with skateboarding.

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.480
It's Tony Hawk.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:19.580
ANNOUNCER: Legendary Tony Hawk.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.070
 Tony Hawk!

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.020
TONY HAWK: I was 14 years
old when I went pro.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.970
The very first
time that I created

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:32.189
a new trick, that was the buzz.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:34.470
That was the high that I
chased the rest of my life.

00:00:34.470 --> 00:00:38.520
Skateboarding is a lifestyle,
a sport, and an art form

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:39.090
all at once.

00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.990
In this MasterClass,
I am breaking down

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:47.300
foundational skate tricks and
some of my own signature tricks

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.440
for the very first time.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:50.940
We're going to start from the
very beginning, the first time

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:52.370
you step on the skateboard.

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:55.520
The first step of the ollie is
pushing down on your back foot

00:00:55.520 --> 00:00:57.830
until the tail just
hits the ground.

00:00:57.830 --> 00:01:01.340
And that sends your
board straight up.

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:02.540
It feels magical.

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.022
You did this with your feet.

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:06.230
The three types of skateboarding
that we are covering

00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:08.960
are street, park, and vert.

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.300
Lizzie Armanto will take
you to the next level

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:12.950
of intermediate tricks
in park skating.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:16.790
And Riley Hawk will guide you
through complicated and technical

00:01:16.790 --> 00:01:17.960
street tricks.

00:01:17.960 --> 00:01:21.320
The key to a McTwist
is in the snap.

00:01:21.320 --> 00:01:25.880
I reach down for my board, and
I turn my head, immediately

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:26.722
snapping it.

00:01:26.722 --> 00:01:29.180
If you have the snap, you have
the grab, you have the spin,

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:29.780
you can do it.

00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:31.520
It's just one that you
didn't get to see the landing

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:32.353
zone the whole time.

00:01:36.710 --> 00:01:39.920
School was not a
pleasant experience.

00:01:39.920 --> 00:01:41.750
I got picked on a lot.

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.550
And then I skated.

00:01:43.550 --> 00:01:49.170
When I found skateboarding,
I found my voice.

00:01:49.170 --> 00:01:52.320
You don't have to follow
the textbook of exactly

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.550
how to live your life.

00:01:53.550 --> 00:01:56.940
Skateboarding can be a
great lesson in your life,

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:00.270
a lesson in perseverance, a
lesson in self-confidence,

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.900
a lesson in belief.

00:02:02.900 --> 00:02:04.550
You don't have to
be a pro skater.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:06.920
But you can carry
these lessons with you

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:09.830
throughout your life
in so many other ways.

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:13.630
I'm Tony Hawk, and
this is my MasterClass.

